    ]
  },
  "scope_notes": "Roughly 95% of the diff is test code, unit test vectors, JSON test data files (bip54_timestamps.json and bip54_coinbases.json), and fuzz testing. Consensus-critical logic changes are confined to src/consensus/ and src/validation.cpp.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Rebased with minor test adjustments, such as separating 63-byte and 64-byte functional tests and updating functional test framework coinbase creation scripts.",
  "card": "This PR implements BIP 54 (Consensus Cleanup) validation rules, configured as active exclusively on regtest and never active on mainnet, testnet, or signet. The soft fork rules mitigate legacy sigops CPU exhaustion by capping non-witness sigops at 2,500 per transaction, invalidate 64-byte transactions to prevent Merkle tree collisions, require coinbases to be timelocked to block height minus one, and restrict block timestamps to prevent timewarp and negative difficulty adjustments. Over 95% of the diff consists of test vectors, unit tests, a fuzzing target, and functional tests ported and improved from Bitcoin Inquisition. This enables full in-tree testing and review of the consensus cleanup proposal without altering consensus rules on live networks.",
